// =====================================================================
// SCENE 7 · DAY 4: CORNERED
// Anin's friends start noticing the loop, and every sign points back to
// her. Fal asks if she ever feels like they keep missing tomorrow. That
// night, she stays awake.
//
// NOTES FOR THE PROGRAMMER
// - Every "//" comment is a stage direction for you, not in-game text.
// - Commands used (same as before, plus):
//     <<cutscene "id">>, <<npc_enter>>, <<npc_exit>>, <<advance_time>>,
//     <<event_marker>>, <<scene_transition>>, <<quest_start>>,
//     <<quest_update>>, <<enable_control>>
//     <<stay_awake "success">>  screen dims and recovers twice, the
//                               clock reaches 23:59, Anin is still awake
// - TRUTH FLAGS: $truth_dira, $truth_lila, $truth_kirana, $truth_fal.
//   Dira/Lila/Kirana are OPTIONAL talks after lunch, before the bell.
//   Fal's is set in the required library scene. They only change
//   Anin's dialogue options in Scene 8. Chapter 1 always ends with the
//   loop continuing.
// - World state from Gap 3: Kirana's calendar shows "10" on every date
//   except the circled 12th ("Ferry, 06:00"). Dira's book has a margin
//   note. Lila's sketchbook is full of Warmus lunches.
// =====================================================================


// ---------------------------------------------------------------------
// DORM — MORNING
// Kirana is standing by the calendar.
// ---------------------------------------------------------------------

title: Day4_Start
tags: scene7 day4 dorm
---
<<set $truth_dira to false>>
<<set $truth_lila to false>>
<<set $truth_kirana to false>>
<<set $truth_fal to false>>
<<npc_enter "Kirana">>
Kirana: Anin. Did you do this?
-> Do what?
-> ...
Kirana: Every day. Every single day says ten. Even the weekends.
<<enable_control>>
<<quest_start "day4" "Look at the calendar">>
// Interactable: Day4_Calendar (required)
===

title: Day4_Calendar
tags: scene7 day4 dorm interactable required
---
Anin: Every date is the tenth. Except one. The twelfth is circled. "Ferry, 06:00."
Anin: Kirana... you're leaving?
Kirana: ...I was going to tell you after graduation. My parents found work back home. Three islands away.
Kirana: Don't look at me like that. It's not like I'm dying.
Kirana: Whatever. Someone's being weird. Let's just go.
<<npc_exit "Kirana">>
<<quest_update "day4" "Go to class">>
<<scene_transition "Classroom">>
<<jump Day4_Classroom>>
===


// ---------------------------------------------------------------------
// CLASSROOM — MORNING
// ---------------------------------------------------------------------

title: Day4_Classroom
tags: scene7 day4 classroom event
---
// Dira is staring at her open book.
Dira: Anin. Come here.
Dira: Someone wrote in my book. "You've read this before."
Dira: This is your handwriting.
-> It's not—
-> I don't remember writing it.
Dira: That's not a no.
<<npc_enter "Lila">>
// Lila bursts in, sketchbook in hand.
Lila: Guys. Guys. Look.
Lila: I didn't draw these. I don't remember drawing these. But it's my sketchbook, and it's... us. At Warmus.
// Interactable: Day4_Sketchbook (required)
===

title: Day4_Sketchbook
tags: scene7 day4 classroom interactable required
---
Anin: Page after page. The same lunch. Same table.
// First time day Anin says "she". She's starting to suspect it isn't
// just sleepwalking.
Anin: I didn't draw these. She did.
Kirana: Okay. This is a prank. Right? Anin?
<<advance_time "lunch">>
<<scene_transition "Cafeteria">>
<<jump Day4_Lunch>>
===


// ---------------------------------------------------------------------
// CAFETERIA — LUNCH (required)
// ---------------------------------------------------------------------

title: Day4_Lunch
tags: scene7 day4 cafeteria event
---
<<cutscene "day4_lunch_matches">>
// The lunch from Lila's drawings plays out exactly as drawn: same seats,
// same nasi goreng. Lila holds the sketchbook up beside the real table.
// They match.
Lila: ...It's the same.
Dira: Anin, you always know what we're going to say. You always know what's coming. You know what I'm reading. You're not even surprised right now.
Kirana: You finish my sentences too. Like you already heard them.
Kirana: Why does it feel like we've had this exact conversation before?
-> Because we have.
    Anin: ...Forget it. I didn't mean that.
-> I don't know.
Dira: What's happening to us?
// Anin is cornered. No choice gets her out of it cleanly.
<<quest_update "day4" "Meet Fal at the library after school">>
// OPTIONAL: before the bell, the player can talk to each friend alone.
// Day4_Talk_Dira, Day4_Talk_Lila, Day4_Talk_Kirana. Each sets a truth
// flag. Interacting with the library door advances time.
===


// ---------------------------------------------------------------------
// OPTIONAL TALKS (before the bell)
// ---------------------------------------------------------------------

title: Day4_Talk_Dira
tags: scene7 day4 optional
---
Dira: The letter's still in my bag. I keep thinking: if I never open it, I never have to find out. And I never have to leave.
<<set $truth_dira to true>>
===

title: Day4_Talk_Lila
tags: scene7 day4 optional
---
Lila: The drawing for after graduation? I keep starting it over. It never feels finished. Like there's no "after" to draw.
<<set $truth_lila to true>>
===

title: Day4_Talk_Kirana
tags: scene7 day4 optional
---
Kirana: Three islands away. I'm scared I'll forget what you all sound like.
<<set $truth_kirana to true>>
===


// ---------------------------------------------------------------------
// LIBRARY — AFTER SCHOOL (required)
// Fal is already at the table, books open.
// ---------------------------------------------------------------------

title: Day4_Library
tags: scene7 day4 library event
---
<<advance_time "after_school">>
<<npc_enter "Fal">>
Fal: You look worse than me, and I'm the one failing math.
Fal: Can I ask you something weird?
Fal: Do you ever feel like we keep missing tomorrow?
-> Every day.
-> What do you mean?
Fal: Like it's always about to happen. Graduation, my dad's plan, whatever comes after. And it just... doesn't come.
Fal: Sometimes I'm glad. Sometimes it feels like being stuck.
<<set $truth_fal to true>>
<<npc_exit "Fal">>
<<scene_transition "Dorm">>
<<jump Day4_Dorm_Night>>
===


// ---------------------------------------------------------------------
// DORM — NIGHT
// Kirana is asleep. Anin sits at the window with all the lights on.
// ---------------------------------------------------------------------

title: Day4_Dorm_Night
tags: scene7 day4 dorm
---
Anin: Not tonight. Whoever she is, I'm going to see her.
<<stay_awake "success">>
// MIDNIGHT: the gap begins with Anin AWAKE.
// TRANSITION → Scene 8 (do NOT play the normal gap intro)
// No white flash. The Dorm reloads at midnight with Gap4_Start as its
// start node, and Gap4_Start plays the awake gap intro.
<<set $chapter_scene to 8>>
<<soft_reset>>
===
